/-!
# The degree-one Hasse principle at the involutive subgroup, for a `ℤ`-lattice coefficient
-/

open CategoryTheory

noncomputable section

namespace Work.SSGRoute.ExtChain

/-- **The degree-one Hasse principle at the involutive subgroup, for a `ℤ`-lattice coefficient.**

`H = ⟨σ̄⟩ ≤ G = Gal(K/k)` is generated by `σ̄ = res k K σ` and has order `2` (`hnt : σ̄ ≠ 1`,
`hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1`); it is the full Galois group of `K / K^{σ̄}`.  For a `ℤ`-lattice `M` (finite, free
over `ℤ`) with an `H`-action, the coefficient change `Kˣ → 𝕀_K` makes `Ext¹_H(M, Kˣ) → Ext¹_H(M, 𝕀_K)`
injective.  Since `M` is `ℤ`-free, `Ext¹_H(M,A) = H¹(H, Hom_ℤ(M,A))` exactly (no spectral sequence,
no `d₂`), so this is the Hasse principle for `H¹(H, Hom_ℤ(M,Kˣ))`; by the long exact sequence of
`0 → Kˣ → 𝕀_K → C_K → 0` it is equivalent to the surjectivity of
`H⁰(H, Hom_ℤ(M,𝕀_K)) → H⁰(H, Hom_ℤ(M,C_K))`.

The two classical shapes are on disk: `c` acting by the Galois action gives `H¹(H,Kˣ) = 0`
(Hilbert 90); the action `u ↦ c(u)^{-1}` gives
`H¹(H,Kˣ) = (K^{σ̄})ˣ/Nm_{K/K^{σ̄}}(Kˣ) ↪ (𝕀_K)^{σ̄}/Nm(𝕀_K)` (Hasse's norm theorem,
`NK.GlobalCFTdeep.cyclicHasseInput.hasse_norm`), and the `ℤ`-coefficient relative Hasse–Brauer–Noether
statement is `NK.GlobalCFTdeep.hbnUnits`.  Caveat: a general `ℤ`-lattice with a `C₂`-action need not
split into its `±1`-eigenspaces (`M = ℤ²`, `c(x,y) = (x+y,-y)`: `[M : M₊ ⊕ M₋] = 2`), so
`Hom_ℤ(M,Kˣ)` is an extension of the two classical pieces by a `2`-torsion quotient and the reduction
to them is not free.  (An orphaned file `Submission/Work/SSGRoute/ExtChain/hasseExt1_C2_lattice.lean`
already carries this statement with a `sorry`; proving it here, sorry-free, retires that orphan.) -/
theorem hasseExt1_C2_lattice_general (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (k Ω : Type) [Field k] [NumberField k]
    [Field Ω] [Algebra k Ω] [IsAlgClosure k Ω] (K : IntermediateField k Ω)
    [FiniteDimensional k K] [IsGalois k K] [NumberField K]
    (σ : Ω ≃ₐ[k] Ω) (hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1) (hnt : SSGRoute.res k K σ ≠ 1)
    (M : Rep.{0} SSGRoute.PTExt.Coeff ↥(Subgroup.zpowers (SSGRoute.res k K σ)))
    [Module.Finite ℤ M.V] [Module.Free ℤ M.V] :
    ∀ z : CategoryTheory.Abelian.Ext.{0} M
        (Rep.res (Subgroup.zpowers (SSGRoute.res k K σ)).subtype (SSGRoute.PTExt.unitsK k ↥K)) 1,
      z.comp (CategoryTheory.Abelian.Ext.mk₀
          (Rep.resMap (Subgroup.zpowers (SSGRoute.res k K σ)).subtype
            (NK.HassePrinciple.ideleIncl k ↥K))) (add_zero 1) = 0 → z = 0 := by
  refine c2_extOne_injective_of_surj (S := c2SES (K := K) σ) (c2SES_shortExact (K := K) σ)
    (X := M) ?_
  intro c
  exact c2_lattice_lift (K := K) σ hσ hnt M c

end Work.SSGRoute.ExtChain
